# What the image does not need. Added when a second cargo build joined the
# first: `COPY . .` was carrying 9.5 GB of build output and basemap into the
# daemon on every build, and the new stage doubled the worst of it.
#
# Nothing here is read during the build. The basemap and the heightmap are
# *mounted* at run time (see docker-compose.yml), never copied -- the image is
# deliberately small and the 1.7 GB archive lives outside it.

# Build output, both workspaces. The image compiles its own.
target/
ai-sdk/target/

# The basemap. Bind-mounted, and larger than everything else together.
map-data/

# History. No build step reads it, and it is the second largest thing here.
.git/

# Notes and scratch that are not part of the program.
SESSION.md
ai-sdk/HANDOFF.md
ai-sdk/DESIGN.md
data/visits.jsonl
*.gif
*.jpeg

# Not excluding `moonin/`, though nothing in the image uses it: the root
# `Cargo.toml` lists it as a workspace member, so cargo refuses to load the
# workspace at all without its manifest. Tried it; the build fails on the
# *portfolio* stage with "failed to read /src/moonin/Cargo.toml", which reads
# like a problem with this change and is not.

# Credentials never belong in a build context.
.env
